# ---- Local Supabase (recommended for development & demos) ----
# 1. Install Docker Desktop and the Supabase CLI (`npm i -g supabase` or see
#    https://supabase.com/docs/guides/local-development/cli/getting-started).
# 2. From this directory: `supabase start` (first run pulls Docker images and
#    can take a few minutes; it also seeds a working admin login and sample
#    departments/positions — see supabase/seed.sql).
# 3. Copy this file to `.env` and use the values below — they are Supabase's
#    fixed local-dev defaults, not secrets, and are safe to commit/share.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:55321
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZS1kZW1vIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJleHAiOjE5ODM4MTI5OTZ9.CRXP1A7WOeoJeXxjNni43kdQwgnWNReilDMblYTn_I0

# Sign in with: admin@suite.com / Admin123 (seeded by supabase/seed.sql).

# ---- Remote (cloud) Supabase project ----
# Project Settings > API in the Supabase dashboard. Uncomment and fill in to
# point this app at a hosted project instead of your local stack.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# The origin this app is served from. Used to build redirect URLs for Supabase
# Auth flows (e.g. HR account invitations land on {VITE_SITE_URL}/auth/setup-password).
# Must also be added to Authentication > URL Configuration > Redirect URLs in the
# Supabase dashboard (already the case for the local stack — see supabase/config.toml),
# or Supabase will silently fall back to the Site URL instead.
#
# Development:
VITE_SITE_URL=http://localhost:5173
# Production (set this in your Vercel project's Environment Variables instead):
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://your-app.vercel.app
